    narr:narration """A cutover-review call that opens with [a correction offered at the top rather than buried](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_1): the analyst who had set [a two-week soak between sites, now retracted as wrong](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_3) walks the room through [the Dockside log re-analysis behind it](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_5) — the nine-day exception queue was an artifact of [a weekly reconciliation job retired in July](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_7), not a property of the site. From that she proposes [a revised one-week soak](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_9), while the lead confirms [the sequential one-site-at-a-time plan does not move](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_10). The expert voices the cost: [the new number is defensible but has no slack](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_13), and asks it [be on the record as tight, not safe](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_15). The lead accepts the trade, notes [three weeks recovered across four sites](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_17), allocates it [to the Clyde buffer](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_18), and [ratifies the supersession formally](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_20) before tasking [a write-up for the steering group](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_22), closing on [why it was brought rather than let ride](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_24).""" ;
